AB  - Welcome from the ChairsWelcome to the 2nd edition of the International Workshop on Software Security Testing (SECUTE 2026), focusing on security testing of software systems.The workshop was held on October 16, 2026, at the Holiday Inn Munich -City Center in Munich, Germany, co-located with ASE 2026.Following the first edition in 2024, SECUTE 2026 aims to build a community where researchers and practitioners can discuss new ideas and share fresh insights on software security testing.SECUTE places particular emphasis on innovative automated techniques and methods to support the creation, management, and evolution of automated tests that detect security flaws in source code.This also includes evaluating existing security testing approaches, understanding the current state of security testing practices, and defining key challenges and a roadmap for future research in the field.The event hosted a thematic talk by Prof. Jürgen Cito from TU Wien, Austria, titled "Language Models as Penetration Testing Agents: Surprising Capabilities and Ethical Dimensions", which presented how LLMs reason and operate in penetration testing compared to human testers and discussed ethical concerns.Afterward, the authors of each accepted paper gave a technical talk describing their respective work.Finally, a plenary session discussed the relevance of software security testing and future research directions.SECUTE received nine submissions; seven met the requirements and were sent to three program committee members for review.After online discussions, the committee ultimately accepted five papers (71% acceptance rate).The workshop chairs thank the program committee, the web and publicity chair, the keynote speaker, the paper authors, and the ASE 2026 organizers for making this event possible and successful.
